  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "p13-selected-regime",
      "basis": "source_statement",
      "locator": {
        "pdf_pages": [
          9,
          10
        ],
        "section_equations": "SectionIII.A.3,Eq46-48 and supersymmetric three27 paragraph"
      },
      "fact": "The paper explicitly considers an E6-inspired GSM×U1 construction, not a full E6 GUT. It specifies the supersymmetric model with three complete27 chiral multiplets and allows a Hu,Hd pair inside these27s to serve as MSSM Higgs. This accepted target narrows the earlier uninstantiated charge template to the source-explicit psi benchmark theta=pi/2."
    },
    {
      "id": "p13-weights",
      "basis": "source_statement_and_Dynkin_conversion",
      "locator": {
        "pdf_pages": [
          9,
          11
        ],
        "section_equations": "TableII decomposition/psi column;SectionIII.A.3 field definitions"
      },
      "fact": "Use primitive qpsi=2sqrt(6)Qpsi. Each16 has qpsi=1; each10 has qpsi=-2; singletS has qpsi=4. The16 decomposes to Q,u^c,e^c,d^c,L,nu^c; the10 to D,D^c,Hu,Hd. Source D is colour3,Y=-1/3 and Dc its conjugate; Hu,Hd are weak doublets,Y=+/-1/2. Every such chiral multiplet occurs3times. Exact A2 weights distinguish3 andbar3; A1doublet=[1]."
    },
    {
      "id": "p13-component-counts",
      "basis": "supersymmetry_and_shared_normalization_derivation",
      "locator": {
        "pdf_pages": [
          9,
          10,
          11
        ],
        "section_equations": "Supersymmetric version and scalar-partner statements"
      },
      "fact": "Each source chiral multiplet contributes one source complex scalar and one LH Weyl. Include the four gauge-factor gauginos as adjoint LH Weyl fields, not gauge connections. Hypercharge qY=6Y and qpsi=2sqrt(6)Qpsi are each primitive across full spectrum. Scalar real-module orientation conjugates all factors simultaneously when required."
    },
    {
      "id": "p13-optional-not-added",
      "basis": "source_statement",
      "locator": {
        "pdf_pages": [
          10
        ],
        "section_equations": "Paragraph discussing simple gauge unification"
      },
      "fact": "The additionalHu+Huc pair from an incomplete27+27bar is an optional repair of simple unification. It is not in the explicitly preceding three-complete27 model. Failure of simple gauge unification is not an atlas exclusion criterion. OtherE6benchmarks/nonSUSYcompletions are not united with this inventory."
    }
  ],
